msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:16
msgid ""
"Zenoh is an open source communication protocol and middleware for efficient "
"data distribution across heterogeneous ROS systems. This article describes "
"how to install ``rmw_zenoh_cpp``, select it as your active RMW "
"implementation, and verify communication with a Zenoh router. After you "
"follow these steps, you can run ROS nodes using Zenoh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:20
msgid ""
"Zenoh is an open source communication protocol and middleware designed to "
"facilitate efficient data distribution across heterogeneous systems. It "
"provides location-transparent abstractions for high performance pub/sub and "
"distributed queries. See also: https://zenoh.io/docs/getting-started/first-"
"app/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:30
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:33
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:35
msgid ""
"Have :doc:`rosdep installed <../../../../ROS-Framework/client-libraries/"
"Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:38
msgid "Installation packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:40
msgid ""
"The rmw implementation Zenoh can be installed via binaries, recommended for "
"stable development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:42
msgid ""
"Binary packages for supported ROS 2 distributions (see distro branches) are "
"available on respective Tier-1 platforms for the distributions. First ensure "
"that your system is set up to install ROS 2 binaries by following the "
"instructions here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:45
msgid "Then install rmw_zenoh binaries using the command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:47
msgid "sudo apt install ros-rolling-rmw-zenoh-cpp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:52
msgid "Build from source code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:54
msgid "Building from source is only recommended if latest features are needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:56
msgid ""
"By default, we vendor and compile ``zenoh-cpp`` with a subset of zenoh "
"features. The ``ZENOHC_CARGO_FLAGS`` CMake argument may be overwritten with "
"other features included if required. See `zenoh_cpp_vendor/CMakeLists.txt "
"<https://github.com/ros2/rmw_zenoh/blob/rolling/zenoh_cpp_vendor/CMakeLists."
"txt>`__ for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:60
msgid "Clone the repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:62
msgid ""
"mkdir ~/ws_rmw_zenoh/src -p && cd ~/ws_rmw_zenoh/src\n"
"git clone https://github.com/ros2/rmw_zenoh.git -b rolling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:67
msgid "Install dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:69
msgid ""
"cd ~/ws_rmw_zenoh\n"
"rosdep install --from-paths src --ignore-src --rosdistro rolling -y"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:74
msgid "Build the workspace using Colcon:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:76
msgid ""
"source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash\n"
"colcon build --cmake-args -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:82
msgid "Switch to rmw_zenoh_cpp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:84
msgid ""
"Switch from other rmw to rmw_zenoh_cpp by specifying the environment "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:86
msgid "export RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_zenoh_cpp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:91
msgid "Run the talker and listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:93
msgid "Now run ``talker`` and ``listener`` to test Zenoh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:95
msgid "Start the Zenoh router"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:97
msgid ""
"# terminal 1\n"
"source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash\n"
"ros2 run rmw_zenoh_cpp rmw_zenohd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:103
msgid ""
"Without the Zenoh router, nodes will not be able to discover each other "
"since multicast discovery is disabled by default in the node's session "
"config. Instead, nodes will receive discovery information about other peers "
"via the Zenoh router's gossip functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:106
msgid ""
"# terminal 2\n"
"export RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_zenoh_cpp\n"
"source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash\n"
"ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:113
msgid ""
"# terminal 3\n"
"export RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_zenoh_cpp\n"
"source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash\n"
"ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations/Non-DDS-Implementations/Working-with-Zenoh.rst:120
msgid ""
"Remember to source your ROS 2 setup script before running these commands."
msgstr ""
